03","status":"p","title":"The Lancet Respiratory Medicine","title_org":"The lancet. Respiratory medicine","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85169037378"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-f3dcf768-7e61-4a8e-a51f-303c0e123611"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Intravenous aviptadil and remdesivir for treatment of COVID-19-associated hypoxaemic respiratory failure in the USA (TESICO) : a randomised, placebo-controlled trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-732850","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background: Increasing SERCA2 (sarco[endo]-plasmic reticulum Ca2+ ATPase 2) activity is suggested to be beneficial in chronic heart failure, but no selective SERCA2-activating drugs are available. PDE3A (phosphodiesterase 3A) is proposed to be present in the SERCA2 interactome and limit SERCA2 activity. Disruption of PDE3A from SERCA2 might thus be a strategy to develop SERCA2 activators Methods: Confocal microscopy, 2-color direct stochastic optical reconstruction microscopy, proximity ligation assays, immunoprecipitations, peptide arrays, and surface plasmon resonance were used to investigate colocalization between SERCA2 and PDE3A in cardiomyocytes, map the SERCA2/PDE3A interaction sites, and optimize disruptor peptides that release PDE3A from SERCA2. Functional experiments assessing the effect of PDE3A-binding to SERCA2 were performed in cardiomyocytes and HEK293 vesicles. The effect of SERCA2/PDE3A disruption by the disruptor peptide OptF (optimized peptide F) on cardiac mortality and function was evaluated during 20 weeks in 2 consecutive randomized, blinded, and controlled preclinical trials in a total of 148 mice injected with recombinant adeno-associated virus 9 (rAAV9)-OptF, rAAV9-control (Ctrl), or PBS, before undergoing aortic banding (AB) or sham surgery and subsequent phenotyping with serial echocardiography, cardiac magnetic resonance imaging, histology, and functional and molecular assays Results: PDE3A colocalized with SERCA2 in human nonfailing, human failing, and rodent myocardium. Amino acids 277-402 of PDE3A bound directly to amino acids 169-216 within the actuator domain of SERCA2. Disruption of PDE3A from SERCA2 increased SERCA2 activity in normal and failing cardiomyocytes. SERCA2/PDE3A disruptor peptides increased SERCA2 activity also in the presence of protein kinase A inhibitors and in phospholamban-deficient mice, and had no effect in mice with cardiomyocyte-specific inactivation of SERCA2. Cotransfection of PDE3A reduced SERCA2 activity in HEK293 vesicles. Treatment with rAAV9-OptF reduced cardiac mortality compared with rAAV9-Ctrl (hazard ratio, 0.26 [95% CI, 0.11 to 0.63]) and PBS (hazard ratio, 0.28 [95% CI, 0.09 to 0.90]) 20 weeks after AB. Mice injected with rAAV9-OptF had improved contractility and no difference in cardiac remodeling compared with rAAV9-Ctrl after aortic banding. Conclusions: Our results suggest that PDE3A regulates SERCA2 activity through direct binding, independently of the catalytic activity of PDE3A. Targeting the SERCA2/PDE3A interaction prevented cardiac mortality after AB, most likely by improving cardiac contractility.","author_count":25,"contributors":["Skogestad, Jonas","Albert, Ingrid","Hougen, Karina","Lothe, Gustav B.","Lunde, Marianne","Eken, Olav Søvik","Veras, Ioanni","Huynh, Ngoc Trang Thi","Børstad, Mira","Marshall, Serena","Shen, Xin","Louch, William E.","Robinson, Emma Louise","Cleveland, Joseph C.","Ambardekar, Amrut V.","Schwisow, Jessica A.","Jonas, Eric","Calejo, Ana I.","Morth, Jens Preben","Taskén, Kjetil","Melleby, Arne Olav","Lunde, Per Kristian","Sjaastad, Ivar","Carlson, Cathrine Rein","Aronsen, Jan Magnus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-669215"],"filters":{"added":"2023-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Aronsen, Jan Magnus"],"country":["Norway","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Oslo University Hospital","University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus","University of Oslo"],"keyword":["Calcium","Excitation contraction coupling","Heart failure","Phosphodiesterase"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"disruption of phosphodiesterase 000000000003a binding to serca000000000002 increases serca000000000002 activity and reduces mortality in mice with chronic heart failure","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85152631026","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-669215","identifier":[{"id":"36876489","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85152631026","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-3727075b-b7e5-44e3-a6a5-a0d71b046174"],"keyword":["Calcium","Excitation contraction coupling","Heart failure","Phosphodiesterase","Sarco-endoplasmic reticulum Ca2+-ATPase"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B6A9872052D79BB2128C91F77986B4C3"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"no","key":"oslo university hospital","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Oslo University Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"no","key":"university of oslo","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Oslo","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"university of colorado anschutz medical campus","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Centers, DTU Microbes Initiative","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Biotechnology and Biomedicine","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Biotechnology and Biomedicine, Section for Protein Chemistry and Enzyme Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Biotechnology and Biomedicine, Section for Protein Chemistry and Enzyme Technology, DTU Structural Biology Core","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Biotechnology and Biomedicine, Section for Protein Chemistry and Enzyme Technology, Structural Enzymology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas","key":"skogestadjonaspau","last":"Skogestad","name":"Skogestad, Jonas","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ingrid","key":"albertingridpau","last":"Albert","name":"Albert, Ingrid","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Karina","key":"hougenkarinapau","last":"Hougen","name":"Hougen, Karina","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Gustav B.","key":"lothegustavbpau","last":"Lothe","name":"Lothe, Gustav B.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marianne","key":"lundemariannepau","last":"Lunde","name":"Lunde, Marianne","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Olav Søvik","key":"ekenolavsøvikpau","last":"Eken","name":"Eken, Olav Søvik","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ioanni","key":"verasioannipau","last":"Veras","name":"Veras, Ioanni","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ngoc Trang Thi","key":"huynhngoctrangthipau","last":"Huynh","name":"Huynh, Ngoc Trang Thi","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mira","key":"børstadmirapau","last":"Børstad","name":"Børstad, Mira","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Serena","key":"marshallserenapau","last":"Marshall","name":"Marshall, Serena","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xin","key":"shenxinpau","last":"Shen","name":"Shen, Xin","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"William E.","key":"louchwilliamepau","last":"Louch","name":"Louch, William E.","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Emma Louise","key":"robinsonemmalouisepau","last":"Robinson","name":"Robinson, Emma Louise","rank":13,"rolec