:"Fogliatto, Laura M.","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","first":"Carsten U.","key":"niemannpau","last":"Niemann","locid":"c34cbf81-3f48-4443-8481-b428de733daa","name":"Niemann, Carsten Utoft","name_org":"Niemann, Carsten U.","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"9","first":"Robert","key":"weinkovepau","last":"Weinkove","name":"Weinkove, Robert","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"10","first":"Sue","key":"robinsonpau","last":"Robinson","name":"Robinson, Sue","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"11","first":"Thomas J.","key":"kippspau","last":"Kipps","name":"Kipps, Thomas J.","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"12","first":"Eugen","key":"tauschpau","last":"Tausch","name":"Tausch, Eugen","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"13","first":"William","key":"scharypau","last":"Schary","name":"Schary, William","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"14","first":"Matthias","key":"ritgenpau","last":"Ritgen","name":"Ritgen, Matthias","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"15","first":"Clemens Martin","key":"wendtnerpau","last":"Wendtner","name":"Wendtner, Clemens Martin","rank":21,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Karl Anton","key":"kreuzerpau","last":"Kreuzer","name":"Kreuzer, Karl Anton","rank":22,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Barbara","key":"eichhorstpau","last":"Eichhorst","name":"Eichhorst, Barbara","rank":23,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"12","first":"Stephan","key":"stilgenbauerpau","last":"Stilgenbauer","name":"Stilgenbauer, Stephan","rank":24,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Michael","key":"hallekpau","last":"Hallek","name":"Hallek, Michael","rank":25,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kirsten","key":"fischerpau","last":"Fischer","name":"Fischer, Kirsten","rank":26,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32888452"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/s1470-2045(20)30443-5","issn":["14702045","14745488"],"issn_org":["14702045"],"issue":"9","journal":"The Lancet Oncology","pages":"1188-1200","status":"p","title":"The Lancet Oncology","volume":"21"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85090023171"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-66fcd176-bcc3-4490-bb08-e2e6129ce735"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Venetoclax plus obinutuzumab versus chlorambucil plus obinutuzumab for previously untreated chronic lymphocytic leukaemia (CLL14) : follow-up results from a multicentre, open-label, randomised, phase 3 trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-454933","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: We aimed to describe the extent of neurodevelopmental impairments and identify the genetic etiologies in a large cohort of patients with epilepsy with myoclonic atonic seizures (MAE). METHODS: We deeply phenotyped MAE patients for epilepsy features, intellectual disability, autism spectrum disorder, and attention-deficit/hyperactivity disorder using standardized neuropsychological instruments. We performed exome analysis (whole exome sequencing) filtered on epilepsy and neuropsychiatric gene sets to identify genetic etiologies. RESULTS: We analyzed 101 patients with MAE (70% male). The median age of seizure onset was 34 months (range = 6-72 months). The main seizure types were myoclonic atonic or atonic in 100%, generalized tonic-clonic in 72%, myoclonic in 69%, absence in 60%, and tonic seizures in 19% of patients. We observed intellectual disability in 62% of patients, with extremely low adaptive behavioral scores in 69%. In addition, 24% exhibited symptoms of autism and 37% exhibited attention-deficit/hyperactivity symptoms. We discovered pathogenic variants in 12 (14%) of 85 patients, including five previously published patients. These were pathogenic genetic variants in SYNGAP1 (n = 3), KIAA2022 (n = 2), and SLC6A1 (n = 2), as well as KCNA2, SCN2A, STX1B, KCNB1, and MECP2 (n = 1 each). We also identified three new candidate genes, ASH1L, CHD4, and SMARCA2 in one patient each. SIGNIFICANCE: MAE is associated with significant neurodevelopmental impairment. MAE is genetically heterogeneous, and we identified a pathogenic genetic etiology in 14% of this cohort by exome analysis. These findings suggest that MAE is a manifestation of several etiologies rather than a discrete syndromic entity.","author_count":32,"contributors":["Tang, Shan","Addis, Laura","Smith, Anna","Topp, Simon D","Pendziwiat, Manuela","Mei, Davide","Parker, Alasdair","Agrawal, Shakti","Hughes, Elaine","Lascelles, Karine","Williams, Ruth E","Fallon, Penny","Robinson, Robert","Cross, Helen J","Hedderly, Tammy","Eltze, Christin","Kerr, Tim","Desurkar, Archana","Hussain, Nahin","Kinali, Maria","Bagnasco, Irene","Vassallo, Grace","Whitehouse, William","Goyal, Sushma","Absoud, Michael","Møller, Rikke S.","Helbig, Ingo","Weber, Yvonne G","Marini, Carla","Guerrini, Renzo","Simpson, Michael A","Pal, Deb K"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-632495"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corpau":["EuroEPINOMICS RES Consortium"],"corresponding_author":["Tang, Shan"],"country":["China","Germany","Italy","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["Addenbrooke's Hospital","All Global Affiliations","Children's Hospital of Philadelphia","Eberhard Karls University of Tübingen","Eli Lilly and Company","Evelina London Children's Hospital","Great Ormond Street Hospital","Hertie Institut for Clinical Brain Research, Tübingen, Germany","King's College Hospital","King's College London","Meyer Children’s Hospital","Nottingham University Business School China","Royal Manchester Children's Hospital","UCL Great Ormond Street Institute of Child Health","University of Florence","University of Pennsylvania"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Schleswig-Holstein University Clinics"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"phenotypic and genetic spectrum of epilepsy with myoclonic atonic seizures","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/epi.16508","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-632495","identifier":[{"id":"32469098","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85085582268","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-ced107d7-eec6-4163-b751-20fb01408de7"],"lang":"English","level"