chlinskyarturopau","last":"Zychlinsky","name":"Zychlinsky, Arturo","rank":436,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31633216"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/eji.201970107","issn":["00142980","15214141"],"issn_org":["00142980"],"issue":"10","journal":"European Journal of Immunology","pages":"1457-1973","publisher":"Wiley - VCH Verlag GmbH & Co. KGaA","publisher_org":"Wiley - V C H Verlag GmbH & Co. KGaA","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Immunology","volume":"49"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85073598520"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-94921408-d4c2-405d-94c9-22ee4e4bcb29","ku-9e37d85d-e5a6-4d24-ac2c-5efcd72b831f","sdu-3fcd4576-74a2-44c8-a75a-32906b960113"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Guidelines for the use of flow cytometry and cell sorting in immunological studies (second edition)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-095.40-035982","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Background: The pathophysiology of osteoarthritis (OA) involves wear and tear, and a state of low-grade inflammation. Tissue repair responses include transforming growth factor beta (TGFβ)-induced myofibroblast production of extracellular matrix. Fibronectins are an essential part of the extracellular matrix, and injection of fibronectin fragments into rabbit joints is a previously established animal model of OA. Fibronectin containing the ED-A domain is currently being used as drug delivery target in the development of anti-inflammatory drugs (e.g. Dekavil). Methods: In this study, samples of synovial membrane were obtained from patients with knee OA undergoing joint replacement surgery. Immunostaining for ED-A fibronectin and the myofibroblast marker alpha smooth muscle actin (αSMA) was performed on fibroblast-like synovial cells (FLS) and synovial membranes. RAW 264.7 macrophages were incubated with recombinant ED-A fibronectin. Results: The staining of ED-A fibronectin in OA FLS was increased by TGFβ but not by TNFα, lipopolysaccharide, or IL-6 (n = 3). ED-A fibronectin co-stained with the myofibroblast marker αSMA in both the OA FLS (n = 3) and in the OA synovial membranes (n = 8). ED-A fibronectin staining was associated with both number of lining layer cells (rho = 0.85 and p = 0.011) and sublining cells (rho = 0.88 and p = 0.007) in the OA synovium (n = 8), and co-distributed with TNFα (n = 5). Recombinant ED-A fibronectin increased the production of TNFα by RAW 264.7 macrophages (n = 3). Conclusions: The disease process in OA shares features with the chronic wound healing response. Our findings support utilizing ED-A fibronectin for drug delivery or therapeutic targeting to reduce pro-inflammatory responses in OA.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Kragstrup, Tue Wenzel","Sohn, Dong H","Lepus, Christin M","Onuma, Kazuhiro","Wang, Qian","Robinson, William H","Sokolove, Jeremy"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-174235"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","OECD"],"country":["South Korea","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Pusan National University","Stanford University","VA Palo Alto Healthcare Syst"],"keyword":["Arthritis","Drug delivery","Fibronectin","Inflammation","Myofibroblast","Osteoarthritis","Synovitis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fibroblast like synovial cell production of extra domain a fibronectin associates with inflammation in osteoarthritis","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85081092516","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-174235","identifier":[{"id":"85081092516","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC6886182","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"31819923","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-4ed6fba2-b9bd-462b-9a92-1b0aff266dbc"],"keyword":["Arthritis","Drug delivery","Fibronectin","Inflammation","Myofibroblast","Osteoarthritis","Synoviocyte","Synovitis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B99E0D5B7F1CFE4A9C1CBAE51F3A8CD1"],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Biomedicine, Department of Biomedicine - Forskning og uddannelse, Skou-bygningen","Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Section for Rheumatology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","countr