{"abstract":"HLA-B*46:01 was formed by an intergenic mini-conversion, between HLA-B*15:01 and HLA-C*01:02, in Southeast Asia during the last 50,000 years, and it has since become the most common HLA-B allele in the region. A functional effect of the mini-conversion was introduction of the C1 epitope into HLA-B*46:01, making it an exceptional HLA-B allotype that is recognized by the C1-specific natural killer (NK) cell receptor KIR2DL3. High-resolution mass spectrometry showed that HLA-B*46:01 has a low-diversity peptidome that is distinct from those of its parents. A minority (21%) of HLA-B*46:01 peptides, with common C-terminal characteristics, form ligands for KIR2DL3. The HLA-B*46:01 peptidome is predicted to be enriched for peptide antigens derived from Mycobacterium leprae. Overall, the results indicate that the distinctive peptidome and functions of HLA-B*46:01 provide carriers with resistance to leprosy, which drove its rapid rise in frequency in Southeast Asia.","author_count":20,"contributors":["Hilton, Hugo G.","McMurtrey, Curtis P.","Han, Alex S.","Djaoud, Zakia","Guethlein, Lisbeth A.","Blokhuis, Jeroen H.","Pugh, Jason L.","Goyos, Ana","Horowitz, Amir","Buchli, Rico","Jackson, Ken W.","Bardet, Wilfred","Bushnell, David A.","Robinson, Philip J.","Mendoza, Juan L.","Birnbaum, Michael E.","Nielsen, Morten","Garcia, K. Christopher","Hildebrand, William H.","Parham, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-334887"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Pure Protein, LLC","Stanford University","University of Oklahoma Health Sciences Center"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the intergenic recombinant hla b 000000000046 000000000001 has a distinctive peptidome that includes kir000000000002dl000000000003 ligands","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/134176931/1_s2.0_S2211124717305703_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-334887","identifier":[{"id":"85019206019","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC5510751","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"28514659","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-65a4690b-9389-46d8-9ae2-ebd0f29aab25"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A5376629BA11B56C5C54D4996A231B80"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/134176931/1_s2.0_S2211124717305703_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"stanford university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Stanford University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"university of oklahoma health sciences center","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Oklahoma Health Sciences Center","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"pure protein llc","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Pure Protein, LLC","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Bio and Health Informatics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Bio and Health Informatics, Immunoinformatics and Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hug