versity"],"title":"Fibroblast-like Synovial Cell Production of ED-a Fibronectin Contributes to Inflammation in Osteoarthritis","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-203923","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Gram-negative bacteria possess specialised biogenesis machineries that facilitate the export of amyloid subunits for construction of a biofilm matrix. The secretion of bacterial functional amyloid requires a bespoke outer-membrane protein channel through which unfolded amyloid substrates are translocated. Here, we combine X-ray crystallography, native mass spectrometry, single-channel electrical recording, molecular simulations and circular dichroism measurements to provide high-resolution structural insight into the functional amyloid transporter from Pseudomonas, FapF. FapF forms a trimer of gated β-barrel channels in which opening is regulated by a helical plug connected to an extended coil-coiled platform spanning the bacterial periplasm. Although FapF represents a unique type of secretion system, it shares mechanistic features with a diverse range of peptide translocation systems. Our findings highlight alternative strategies for handling and export of amyloid protein sequences.Gram-negative bacteria assemble biofilms from amyloid fibres, which translocate across the outer membrane as unfolded amyloid precursors through a secretion system. Here, the authors characterise the structural details of the amyloid transporter FapF in Pseudomonas.","author_count":18,"contributors":["Rouse, Sarah L","Hawthorne, William J","Berry, Jamie-Lee","Chorev, Dror S","Ionescu, Sandra A","Lambert, Sebastian","Stylianou, Fisentzos","Ewert, Wiebke","Mackie, Uma","Morgan, R Marc L","Otzen, Daniel","Herbst, Florian-Alexander","Nielsen, Per Halkjær","Dueholm, Morten Simonsen","Bayley, Hagan","Robinson, Carol V","Hare, Stephen","Matthews, Stephen"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-002284"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Asia, South","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Singapore","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Duke-NUS Graduate Medical School","Imperial College London","University of Oxford"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Duke-NUS Medical School, 8 College Road, Singapore, 169857, Singapore."],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a new class of hybrid secretion system is employed in pseudomonas amyloid biogenesis","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-017-00361-6","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-002284","identifier":[{"id":"PMC5557850","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"28811582","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000407553800021","type":"wos"},{"id":"85027511059","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-2d53f2d6-ec99-406d-8bf1-3847fc8d6d15","au-6a46df8e-de7f-4afa-8beb-1b20cbb3cb54"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-67E72638A43C7BF1081153E77D9F41B0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-017-00361-6","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-017-00361-6.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC5557850/pdf/41467_2017_Article_361.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"imperial college london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Imperial College London","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of oxford","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Oxford","used":1},{"affno":"